A||||2||mshill||Instrucions on washing seat covers?||||5
Z||000000||mshill||10-08-1999||02:43 AM||||Every single Fiero I have ever seen has a worn out drivers side upper seat cover, you, know, the place where your butt rubs when you get in the car.  Well, mine has it as well, and I just picked up a pretty clean passenger side upper from the boneyard today to replace my drivers side upper.<P>Are there any special precautions when washing these seat covers? Should I spot clean only, or can I throw it in the washing machine?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-08-1999||09:49 AM||||they will get wrecked in the washer. try spry foam carpet cleaner and a damp sponge.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||10-08-1999||10:26 AM||||Try Chem-Dry Carbonated Stain Extinguisher...about $3 for a canister that will probably clean the entire interior of your car. It's carbonated...floats stains to the surface so they can be blotted up. Drys quickly also. Took all the grease and pop stains out of my carpets and seats. Leaves no residue after drying.<P>I got mine at Menards, but a Home Depot or Lowes should have it.||||reg||10
